{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Or in the flesh.</b> There is no difference between a boil and a burn, and Scripture divided them into two sections to say that half a garis of a boil and half a garis of a burn do not combine to form a whole garis. As stated in tractate Ḥullin: a garis is half a bean, and this is the measurement of impurity for a boil and for a burn."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:11:54.053808070Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}